# The vendored SDK bundle is a GENERATED artifact whose bytes are claimed — PROVENANCE.json records
# its sha256, and scripts/tests/sdk-async-surface.test.js asserts the committed file matches.
#
# Without this rule, git's end-of-line normalisation makes that claim platform-dependent: a Windows
# checkout (autocrlf) rewrites every LF to CRLF, so the same commit produces a different file size
# and a different hash than on Linux or macOS. That is exactly how it was caught — the provenance
# test passed on ubuntu and macOS and failed on windows-latest with a 60-byte difference.
#
# `-text` tells git to store and check this file out verbatim on every platform, which is the
# correct treatment for generated output nobody hand-edits.
cds-maker-sdk.cjs -text
